{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01RkHAx3nsg5JYasdSpR9jUe","type":"tool_result","content":"=== the fix in src/main.rs ===\n\n/// The Rust runtime sets `SIGPIPE` to `SIG_IGN` before `main` is entered, so a\n/// write to a pipe with no reader returns `EPIPE` instead of terminating the\n/// process. The C program never touches the signal, leaving it at `SIG_DFL`, so\n/// the reference dies with `SIGPIPE` (wait status 141) when `printf` writes to a\n/// closed pipe. Restoring the default disposition here keeps the exit status\n/// identical to the C build.\nfn restore_default_sigpipe() {\n    const SIGPIPE: i32 = 13;\n    const SIG_DFL: usize = 0;\n    extern \"C\" {\n        fn signal(signum: i32, handler: usize) -> usize;\n    }\n    unsafe {\n        signal(SIGPIPE, SIG_DFL);\n    }\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    restore_default_sigpipe();\n\n    let mut x: i32 = 0;\n    let mut scanner = Scanner::new();","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37d3bd4f-b219-4e3b-b5e0-33d8e9af55d1","uuid":"241b678b-a325-470c-8783-c11c28e96ea9","timestamp":"2026-08-18T01:44:24.746Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== the fix in src/main.rs ===\n\n/// The Rust runtime sets `SIGPIPE` to `SIG_IGN` before `main` is entered, so a\n/// write to a pipe with no reader returns `EPIPE` instead of terminating the\n/// process. The C program never touches the signal, leaving it at `SIG_DFL`, so\n/// the reference dies with `SIGPIPE` (wait status 141) when `printf` writes to a\n/// closed pipe. Restoring the default disposition here keeps the exit status\n/// identical to the C build.\nfn restore_default_sigpipe() {\n    const SIGPIPE: i32 = 13;\n    const SIG_DFL: usize = 0;\n    extern \"C\" {\n        fn signal(signum: i32, handler: usize) -> usize;\n    }\n    unsafe {\n        signal(SIGPIPE, SIG_DFL);\n    }\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    restore_default_sigpipe();\n\n    let mut x: i32 = 0;\n    let mut scanner = Scanner::new();","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_6y7gj6rwzxtnvkiekzduxgvi2r5rwphujdfbsga3a2zu3avtyh5a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **One real translation bug found and fixed.**\n\n## Important: the task premise didn't match this project\n\nThe instructions describe a multi-feature shared library verified via `libloading`. This project is not that, and I verified the difference mechanically rather than assuming:\n\n- `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` is `add_executable(driver src/main.c)` — **no `.so` exists to load**, on either side.\n- `nm -D` on the C binary shows **zero defined dynamic symbols** — only undefined libc imports (`printf`, `__isoc99_scanf`) and unused weak stubs. There is no exported API to compare.\n- `Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]`** section, and there's no `#[cfg(feature=...)]` anywhere — exactly **one** configuration.\n\nSo symbol parity is trivially 0-vs-0, and there are no feature combinations to cross. Rather than invent `#[no_mangle]` wrappers (which would create an API the C reference doesn't have, testing my harness instead of the translation), I verified the *actual* complete observable surface: `stdin bytes → (stdout, stderr, exit status/signal)`. I added `libloading` as instructed, but documented in `SYMBOLS.md` why it has nothing to open.\n\n## The bug: SIGPIPE disposition\n\nWhen stdout is a pipe with no reader (`driver | true`, or any consumer that exits early):\n\n| | before fix |\n|---|---|\n| C | killed by **signal 13**, wait status 141 |\n| Rust | **exited 0** |\n\nRust's runtime installs `SIG_IGN` for `SIGPIPE` before `main`, so the write returned `EPIPE`, which `let _ = writeln!` silently swallowed. 100% reproducible, both branches, both profiles. Fixed by resetting `SIGPIPE` to `SIG_DFL` at the top of `main`.\n\nI nearly missed this: my first pipe measurement used `PIPESTATUS[0]` under **zsh**, where that array is 1-indexed, so it silently reported `head`'s status instead of the driver's and showed a false match. Re-measuring under bash exposed it.\n\nI **mutation-checked** the regression test — with the fix commented out it fails with exactly the expected diff, so it isn't vacuous.\n\n## What passed\n\n- **41 differential tests**, green in both debug and release, and under `--no-default-features`/`--all-features`.\n- **26 000+ randomized inputs** across two seeds, plus an exhaustive sweep of every integer in `-1000..=1000` and every power of two `2^0..2^67` ±2 — **0 divergences**.\n- The hand-written `scanf(\"%d\")` emulation (the real risk surface — 100 lines of Rust replacing one libc call) matches glibc exactly, including `strtol` saturation-then-truncation: `4294967296` → `0` (flips to `bad()`), `-9223372036854775809` → `LONG_MIN` → low 32 bits `0`.\n- `c_src/` untouched (`main.c` still 60 lines, md5 `5e9ac711…`); only the required `build/` output was added.\n\n## Two caveats worth flagging\n\n1. **`bad()` is undefined behavior.** It dereferences an uninitialized pointer reading a stale stack slot. I verified the C prints `0` stably — 200 repeat runs, varying env padding to shift the stack, and all 19 distinct input routes into that branch — and confirmed via `objdump` that it reads `-0x8(%rbp)`. But the pointer lands in libc's mapped region (not `&x`, which I disproved with a probe), so this stability is a property of *this* compiler/libc/`-O0` build, not a guarantee. The Rust hardcodes `0` to match. A different toolchain could make the C crash or print garbage, and no translation could track that.\n2. One flaky test was my harness's fault, not the translation's: closing the pipe read end *after* `spawn` let an unrelated test's forked child transiently inherit a reader and suppress the signal. Closing it before `spawn` removed the race; I then confirmed stability over 3 consecutive full runs per profile.\n\nArtifacts: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md` (12 rows, all PASS), `CONFIGS.md` (26 rows, all checked), `tests/differential.rs`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":896,"cache_read_input_tokens":96832,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":896,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37d3bd4f-b219-4e3b-b5e0-33d8e9af55d1","uuid":"717bbb07-d3fb-4474-90e4-cd9ad5988762","timestamp":"2026-08-18T01:44:45.653Z"}
